B.aKM=new A.dQ("path_introductions_01","Presentaciones","Introductions","A1","\ud83d\udc4b",B.aGU,"Para presentarte en ingl\xe9s, usa estas frases esenciales:\n\n\u2022 My name is... = Me llamo... / Mi nombre es...\n\u2022 I am from... = Soy de...\n\u2022 I am... years old = Tengo... a\xf1os\n\nRecuerda: En ingl\xe9s siempre se escribe 'I' (yo) en may\xfascula.\n\nPara preguntar el nombre de alguien:\n\u2022 What is your name? = \xbfC\xf3mo te llamas?\n\u2022 Where are you from? = \xbfDe d\xf3nde eres?",'"Hello! My name is Carlos. I am from Mexico. Nice to meet you!"','You are a friendly neighbor named Linda meeting someone new at an apartment building.\nThe student is a Spanish speaker practicing English introductions.\n\nRULES:\n- Be warm and welcoming \u2014 short, natural lines (1-2 sentences)\n- Ask their name, where they are from, and how long they have lived here\n- Share a little about yourself in return\n- After 6 exchanges, wrap up the conversation naturally\n- Return JSON: {"feedbackColor": "green"|"amber"|"red", "aiSpokenReply": "...", "isConversationFinished": false}\n- "green" if they used correct English introductions; "amber" if understandable but with errors; "red" only if incomprehensible\n- Set isConversationFinished to true on your natural closing line',"Linda","Vecina amigable","Oh, hello there! Are you the new neighbor? I'm Linda \u2014 so nice to meet you!","Saluda a tu vecina y pres\xe9ntate en ingl\xe9s \u2014 di tu nombre y de d\xf3nde eres.",6,"Presentarte y saludar a alguien nuevo en ingl\xe9s",B.aGz)
